    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the `frai` CLI where the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through to the `frai-gate` subcommand.\n\n**The Problem:** \nThe `gate` command's action handler was only capturing positional arguments via the `[args...]` parameter, but Commander.js was parsing the `--ci` flag separately and not including it in the `args` array passed to the action.\n\n**The Fix:**\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-755) to extract all arguments (including options) directly from `process.argv` after the `gate` command, ensuring all flags like `--ci` are passed through to the spawned `frai-gate` process.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Built the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Tested `frai gate init --ci` in a fresh directory\n- Confirmed both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created successfully \u2705",
